3. User Personas
Persona 1: Faith Wanjiru — The Busy Undergraduate
Age: 20
Year: 2nd Year, Bachelor of Commerce
Tech comfort: High — uses her phone constantly, comfortable with apps
Context: Faith needs to visit the finance office every semester to clarify a fee statement discrepancy. She has back-to-back lectures and can't afford to lose an hour standing in line.
Goals:
Join the finance office queue without being physically present
Know roughly when to walk over so she doesn't waste time waiting
Get a heads-up notification before her turn
Frustrations:
Has previously stood in line for over an hour only to be told to "come back tomorrow"
Missed her place once after stepping out to buy lunch
Quote: "I just want to know when to actually show up — not stand there the whole time."
Persona 2: Mr. Otieno — The Queue-Facing Staff Member
Age: 45
Role: Registry Officer
Tech comfort: Moderate — comfortable with basic apps and dashboards, not highly technical
Context: Otieno manages the registry front desk during peak registration periods, often dealing with 100+ students in a single day.
Goals:
Easily see who's next and call them forward
Reduce the chaos of students crowding the counter
Mark no-shows and move to the next person quickly
Frustrations:
Physical crowding makes it hard to manage the line fairly
No easy way to communicate delays to waiting students
Quote: "If students knew their position, half of them wouldn't be standing here at all."